{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"identifier":"doc:\/\/TaskLoom\/documentation\/TaskLoom\/AsyncOperation","type":"reference","isActive":true},{"type":"text","text":" accepts a sendable asynchronous closure and returns a sendable result. Every execution runs the closure again. Use "},{"identifier":"doc:\/\/TaskLoom\/documentation\/TaskLoom\/AsyncTask","type":"reference","isActive":true},{"type":"text","text":" for work that returns a value without throwing. Its timeout takes a default value because failure is not part of its result type."}]},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Use "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"map"},{"type":"text","text":" to transform a result and "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"flatMap"},{"type":"text","text":" to select subsequent work. "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"all"},{"type":"text","text":" runs operations concurrently and preserves their input order in the resulting array. "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"allSettled"},{"type":"text","text":" returns an ordered array of "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"Result"},{"type":"text","text":" values, retaining failures and optional successes. Parent cancellation still throws. For bounded scheduling, use "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"collection.concurrentMap(maxConcurrency:)"},{"type":"text","text":"."}]},{"level":2,"text":"Limit concurrent work","type":"heading","anchor":"Limit-concurrent-work"},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Share an "},{"identifier":"doc:\/\/TaskLoom\/documentation\/TaskLoom\/AsyncSemaphore","type":"reference","isActive":true},{"type":"text","text":" between operations and apply "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"limited(by:)"},{"type":"text","text":" to each one. This bounds simultaneous work; it is not a requests-per-second rate limiter. Choose a positive permit count and keep the protected work asynchronous so waiting does not block a thread. Both "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"wait()"},{"type":"text","text":" and "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"withPermit"},{"type":"text","text":" throw when cancelled. Cancelled waiters leave the queue without consuming a permit. Applying "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"limited(by:)"},{"type":"text","text":" to a nonthrowing "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"AsyncTask"},{"type":"text","text":" returns an "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"AsyncOperation"},{"type":"text","text":" because permit acquisition can throw."}]},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"text":"See ","type":"text"},{"type":"reference","identifier":"doc:\/\/TaskLoom\/documentation\/TaskLoom\/CancellationAndRetries","isActive":true},{"text":" before composing timeout, retry, race, and fallback policies.","type":"text"}]}]}],"variants":[{"traits":[{"interfaceLanguage":"swift"}],"paths":["\/documentation\/taskloom\/gettingstarted"]}],"references":{"doc://TaskLoom/documentation/TaskLoom/AsyncSemaphore":{"title":"AsyncSemaphore","identifier":"doc:\/\/TaskLoom\/documentation\/TaskLoom\/AsyncSemaphore","type":"topic","kind":"symbol","navigatorTitle":[{"text":"AsyncSemaphore","kind":"identifier"}],"fragments":[{"text":"actor","kind":"keyword"},{"text":" ","kind":"text"},{"text":"AsyncSemaphore","kind":"identifier"}],"abstract":[{"text":"An actor-based semaphore for limiting concurrent access to a resource.","type":"text"}],"role":"symbol","url":"\/documentation\/taskloom\/asyncsemaphore"},"doc://TaskLoom/documentation/TaskLoom/TaskLifetimes":{"title":"Task lifetimes","identifier":"doc:\/\/TaskLoom\/documentation\/TaskLoom\/TaskLifetimes","type":"topic","kind":"article","abstract":[{"text":"Keep ownership explicit when creating and retaining asynchronous work.","type":"text"}],"role":"article","url":"\/documentation\/taskloom\/tasklifetimes"},"doc://TaskLoom/documentation/TaskLoom/AsyncOperation":{"title":"AsyncOperation","url":"\/documentation\/taskloom\/asyncoperation","type":"topic","kind":"symbol","identifier":"doc:\/\/TaskLoom\/documentation\/TaskLoom\/AsyncOperation","fragments":[{"text":"struct"